      "message": "To clarify, most variable font instances will happen here. FreeType has a hack where indexes greater than 0xFFFF will be interpreted as instance indexes. FontConfig uses this to \"transparently\" present a variable font as a number of instances (much like how ttc indexes work).\n\nIn general one only gets past here with a variable font with FontConfig when requesting a non-named instance. Testing this locally with Skia with the \"Inter Variable\" font installed and using weight 430 early returns below as described and \"works\" in the sense that one gets the default instance.",
